effects_from:
ZzzCharacter.cpp:11310-11343, RenderCharacter's light switch, case MODEL_SHADOW: for every bone that is not a dummy and not 15-20 or 27-32 (the two arms' Box claws), every frame the body is drawn,

    Level 0: CreateSprite(BITMAP_SHINY + 1, Position, 2.5f, Light (1, 1, 1), o, 0.f, 1);
    Level 1: CreateSprite(BITMAP_MAGIC + 1, Position, 0.8f, Light (0.2, 0.7, 0.1), o, 0.f);

and while the action is ATTACK1 or ATTACK2, one reference frame in four, CreateParticle(BITMAP_ENERGY, Position, o->Angle, Light) on each of them. Sprite subtype 1 is EnableAlphaBlendMinus, (ZERO, ONE_MINUS_SRC_COLOR) (ZzzOpenglUtil.cpp:423-431): the Shadow's 39 stars SUBTRACT, a dark X of Shiny02 over every joint. Drawn in game/fx/shadow_stars.h; the bones are found by name (play_open.cpp).

Ours, the user's asks on 2026-10-01 ('more bluryy', 'to active', 'it has to be more subtle', 'more elegant and subtle', 'not its to blurry', 'it also probably be a minimal light emiter'): both sheets blurred at radius 3 (shiny_02_soft, magic_ground_soft in pipeline/index.py); twelve of the body's joints (play_tuning.h kShadowJoints) rather than thirty-nine; the stars at 0.5 of their darkening and the rings at 0.08 of MU's Light; no ENERGY sparks; and the nearest two Poison Shadows a faint green light, 2.5 m.
